	(paper "A1")
	(title_block
		(title "Rails: fused 3V3_MAIN, 3V3_SUP (separate regulators), 5V0_SYS, 3V3_AON; power-on and wake logic, RTC, ready latch and LED")
		(date "2026-11-27")
		(rev "A-draft")
		(company "Open AED project — CERN-OHL-S-2.0 — NOT FOR CONSTRUCTION")
		(comment 1 "NOT FOR CONSTRUCTION — unreviewed design")
		(comment 2 "Source: docs/HARDWARE_DESIGN.md v0.3 §B1.6-B1.8, §B10, §B11; contract.md issue 3 §4, §5.1, §8, §9 (WP-A)")
		(comment 3 "Main and supervisor regulators: separate parts, separate fuses, separate enable networks; the button enables both through separate P-MOSFETs, no logic IC between (D-26)")
		(comment 4 "VBAT_SYS: no steady resistive load below 1 MOhm (contract §4, D-66); lowest on this sheet R316 + R317 = 8.0 MOhm (MAX17320 short-removal test, sheet 01)")
		(comment 5 "3V3_MAIN made here (U301) is used on 01 (battery-load comparator) and 02 (DOCK_RX buffer) as well as 04, 07, 09, 15 (contract issue 3 §4)")
		(comment 6 "Generated by tools/schgen from the sheet spec — edit the spec, not this file (until schematic freeze)")
	)
